{"scenario": {"window_size": "1440x900", "gh": "../fixtures/gh/pr_read.json", "description": "The read side of a GitHub pull request end to end (PLAN §9.9, §9.12 step 4; DESIGN §4.5) against three fixture GitHub clones and mock_gh: each known repository's GitHub name is read beside its listing with no gh call; Ctrl G lists the repository in view's open pull requests (the one asking for the viewer's review first), typing filters and parses a reference without asking gh anything (in the picker and in Ctrl K, the log read before and after), and Enter opens pull request 7; the PR strip shows it (number, title, author, branches, state, checks, round, when it was read), its checks and Open on GitHub go through the system seam to dv's own addresses; GitHub's thread is placed and Resolve resolves it; a push and Ctrl R move the review (\"Updated to 1 new commit\"); a refresh GitHub fails shows in the strip (\"Couldn't refresh · details\"), whole in the main area's banner once asked, and Retry clears it; a pull request's URL typed into Ctrl K is its first row and moves the window to that repository's clone; a reference to a repository dv knows no clone of asks for its folder (cancelled, another repository's clone, no repository, one without GitHub: each says why and adds nothing; then its clone, which opens the pull request and becomes a known repository); the picker says why it has no list (gh not signed in, no open pull requests, a repository that isn't on GitHub) and its field still opens; an open gh refuses is the main area's banner; the switcher lists each repository's PR reviews under \"Pull requests\", and one opened from there shows what was last read of its pull request while GitHub is slow to answer (\"Reading from GitHub…\"); at the window's least width the strip of a pull request with a long title, login and branch, three kinds of checks, a head the closed review didn't follow and a refresh that failed keeps its number, state, checks, round and buttons whole while the rest gives way in order, and the title bar's PRs button is its glyph alone; a list that fails to be read again shows the one read before under why; and after a restart the remembered names match a pasted URL before anything is listed."}}
